From d822042e2cb24fc271792bb2f1ee6132a4e177a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 00:10:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] (thirdparty) ob-kill60 jemalloc with libunwind backtracer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pass `--enable-prof-libunwind` to `build_jemalloc_doris()` so jemalloc's
heap-profile backtracer calls `unw_backtrace` instead of libgcc's
`_Unwind_Backtrace`.

Rationale (different from ck-phdr-unwind, same flag): on glibc >= 2.34
`dlsym` routes through `malloc`. The default libgcc backtracer's
`_Unwind_Backtrace` runs during jemalloc bootstrap and deadlocks
against the `dlsym`-driven malloc. ClickHouse documents this
verbatim in `contrib/jemalloc-cmake/CMakeLists.txt:199-212`; the
text below is the live source comment in the ClickHouse pin Doris's
research mirrors:

    "for JEMALLOC_PROF_LIBGCC it also calls _Unwind_Backtrace()
     during bootstraping of jemalloc, which may lead to deadlock,
     if the dlsym will do allocations somewhere (like glibc does
     prio 2.34)."

ob-kill60 ships no `dl_iterate_phdr` override (no PHDR cache), so the
override-re-entry deadlock that ck-phdr-unwind worries about does
not apply here. The dlsym-bootstrap reason is independent and
applies to every variant that depends on jemalloc on a glibc-2.34
host — which is every Doris BE build on modern Linux.

Detection inputs (CPPFLAGS/LDFLAGS/LIBS) are supplied by the caller's
environment rather than hard-coded, so the patch stays minimal and
the harness wrapper (scripts/phase2/phase2-jemalloc.sh) keeps the
rebuild-scenario plumbing in one place. The wrapper is reused
unchanged from ck-phdr-unwind; its `--enable-prof-libunwind`
sentinel check passes once this patch lands and its md5-keyed cache
hits for the second variant on first invocation.

Post-configure verify of `result: prof-libunwind : 1` in `config.log`
fails early on mismatch: jemalloc/jemalloc#2504 documents detection
silently falling back to libgcc; without the verify the build would
succeed and quietly produce a libgcc-backed archive.

In a fully-clean `build-thirdparty.sh` run, libunwind is built later
in the package list than jemalloc, so a clean invocation of this
function will not yet see libunwind and the verify will fail. The
intended invocation is `build-thirdparty.sh jemalloc_doris` after
the prebuilt thirdparty (which includes libunwind) is in place — the
rebuild scenario the harness wrapper exercises.

Spec: docs/design/ob.md "Decisions" (jemalloc rebuild rationale).
Reference: <ck>/contrib/jemalloc-cmake/CMakeLists.txt:199-212.

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>
---
 thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh b/thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh
index 71a3b38afb8..c6b26f9c789 100755
--- a/thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh
+++ b/thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh
@@ -1613,8 +1613,26 @@ build_jemalloc_doris() {
     # It is not easy to remove `with-jemalloc-prefix`, which may affect the compatibility between third-party and old version codes.
     # Also, will building failed on Mac, it said can't find mallctl symbol. because jemalloc's default prefix on macOS is "je_", not "".
     # Maybe can use alias instead of overwrite.
+    # Reason: `--enable-prof-libunwind` makes jemalloc's heap-profile
+    # backtracer call `unw_backtrace`. On glibc >= 2.34 `dlsym` routes
+    # through `malloc`; the default libgcc backtracer's `_Unwind_Backtrace`
+    # runs during jemalloc bootstrap and deadlocks against the
+    # `dlsym`-driven malloc. Source:
+    # <ck>/contrib/jemalloc-cmake/CMakeLists.txt:199-212.
+    # `CPPFLAGS`/`LDFLAGS`/`LIBS` for libunwind detection come from the
+    # caller's env (see scripts/phase2/phase2-jemalloc.sh).
+    # Spec: docs/design/ob.md "Decisions".
     CFLAGS="${cflags}" ../configure --prefix="${TP_INSTALL_DIR}" --with-install-suffix="_doris" "${WITH_LG_PAGE}" \
-        --with-jemalloc-prefix=je --enable-prof --disable-cxx --disable-libdl --disable-shared
+        --with-jemalloc-prefix=je --enable-prof --enable-prof-libunwind \
+        --disable-cxx --disable-libdl --disable-shared
+
+    # Reason: libunwind detection can silently fall back to libgcc
+    # (jemalloc/jemalloc#2504). Fail before sinking time into `make`.
+    if ! grep -qE "result: prof-libunwind +: 1$" config.log; then
+        echo "ERROR: prof-libunwind != 1 in config.log; libunwind detection failed (jemalloc/jemalloc#2504)." >&2
+        grep -E "result: prof-(libunwind|libgcc|gcc) +:" config.log >&2 || true
+        exit 1
+    fi
 
     make -j "${PARALLEL}"
     make install
